content:
I have reviewed the `BookmarkForm` and identified a synchronization issue caused by the `key={formKey}` in the `DashboardPage`. This was causing the form to remount and lose its state right when the edit data was being passed.

### 1. `formData` State Definition
In `BookmarkForm.tsx`, the state is defined as:
```typescript
const [formData, setFormData] = useState({
  title: initialData?.title || "",
  url: initialData?.url || "",
  is_public: initialData?.is_public ?? false,
});
```

### 2. `useEffect` logic
The `useEffect` is correctly watching `initialData`:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  setFormData({
    title: initialData?.title || "",
    url: initialData?.url || "",
    is_public: initialData?.is_public ?? false,
  });
}, [initialData]);
```

### 3, 4, 5. Input Bindings
The inputs are correctly bound to the state:
- **Title:** `value={formData.title}`
- **URL:** `value={formData.url}`
- **Checkbox:** `checked={formData.is_public}`

### Fix Applied
I removed `key={formKey}` from the `BookmarkForm` in `app/dashboard/page.tsx`. This ensures the component stays mounted and the `useEffect` can smoothly update the `formData` when you click "Edit".

Please try editing a bookmark now; the inputs should populate correctly. If they are still empty, double-check that the bookmark object has exactly the keys `title`, `url`, and `is_public`.

